    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0992" n="890" xml:id="pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">119.2/3017: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-25T12:00:00+01:00">September 25,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 25—7:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>466. My 459, September 20, 5 p.m.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d770-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    states Admiralty is prepared to relay United States Government messages on
                    strictly Government business only between the United States Legation at Addis
                    Ababa and Aden wireless station at Aden from 8:30 to 9:30 a.m. Greenwich mean
                    time. “Frequency will be 10345 kilocycles (slightly under 30 meters wave
                    length).” This service to cost one-half normal rate.</p>
                <p>Should Department accept this proposal Foreign Office suggests further
                    consultation with Embassy as to determining moment when service should
                    commence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
